  "known_limitations": [
    "Licence and publishing organisation for the source are NOT established; the candidate must not be published, uploaded or served until they are.",
    "NOT nationwide: Adamawa, Kano, Katsina, Kebbi, Kwara, Niger, Sokoto, Taraba, Zamfara have no records; 313 of 774 LGA names are absent. A user in those places gets an empty locator.",
    "type is null on every record, so the Mobile consumer's non-emergency filters return nothing until a Product mapping decision is recorded.",
    "emergency_capable is null on every record; emergency ordering degrades to pure distance.",
    "No record in the source was individually verified (every row is a bulk import).",
    "phone is carried in normalised form, but public-use intent for it is not established; no tel: action should be offered before Product review.",
    "10631 source rows without a usable coordinate pair are quarantined, not emitted; they are findable in no build of this candidate.",
    "Exact duplicates are collapsed by a strict rule; looser duplicates (same name and LGA at different points) remain and are counted, not merged.",
    "source_record.lga_id identifies an LGA name, not a state/LGA pair: 11 names carry one id across two states. Key LGAs by (state, city_area), never by lga_id alone.",
    "The source writes latitude and longitude the wrong way round for whole states. 9911 rows were refused on that ground and 81 more as not in the state they claim; FCT, Kano, Katsina, Kwara, Niger, Taraba, Zamfara have no emitted record at all as a result. The rows are listed with both distances; nothing was exchanged. Correction is the source owner's, or an explicitly recorded decision \u2014 not this pipeline's.",
    "The per-state coordinate instrument uses approximate reference points and is uncertain where a state's latitude and longitude are numerically close (Bauchi, Gombe, Yobe, Borno, Kogi): some transposed rows there will have been kept.",
    "In states the evidence reads as predominantly transposed but not emptied (Benue 269, Borno 97, Gombe 346, Jigawa 5, Kaduna 10), the few surviving rows sat close enough to the diagonal to pass the instrument; they are probably transposed too and cannot be told apart from genuine ones.",
    "502 facility names are entirely upper case in the source and are carried as such; re-casing was not applied because it corrupts acronyms (PHC, LUTH). Display casing is a consumer concern.",
    "The artifact is an order of magnitude larger than facilities 1.1; a distribution profile is an open engineering decision."
  ],
